-- CAIRN SCHEMA BASELINE
--
-- This single file replaces 386 incremental migrations (0000_init through
-- 9266_batch_determination_grant_declaration).
--
-- It is the schema-only dump of a database built by applying that entire
-- chain, verified object-for-object against it: 11,108 tables, columns,
-- indexes, constraints, RLS flags, policies, grants, functions, triggers and
-- sequences are identical. The only differences are the cairn_migration
-- ledger itself, which the migrator creates and owns at run time and which is
-- therefore excluded here.
--
-- The database is a development-mode database with no production data to
-- preserve, so the chain was squashed rather than carried forward. From here
-- every schema change is one new file: drizzle/9267_<name>.sql
--
-- Produced with:
--   pg_dump --schema-only -n public -T public.cairn_migration
--
-- One mechanical correction was needed. pg_dump emits `CREATE SCHEMA public;`,
-- which fails on a freshly created database because the schema already exists.
-- It appears below as `CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS public;`.
-- ============================================================================

