ALTER TABLE public.customer_sales_area OWNER TO cairn_integration_migrator;

--
-- Name: COLUMN customer_sales_area.complete_delivery; Type: COMMENT; Schema: public; Owner: cairn_integration_migrator
--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.customer_sales_area.complete_delivery IS 'KNVV-AUTLF. The whole order travels in one delivery, or in none: a delivery that leaves any open item behind is refused. Honoured from this migration; it was maintained and ignored before it.';


--
-- Name: COLUMN customer_sales_area.order_combination; Type: COMMENT; Schema: public; Owner: cairn_integration_migrator
--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.customer_sales_area.order_combination IS 'Whether this customer''s orders may be gathered into one delivery. Honoured from this migration; it was maintained and ignored before it.';


--
-- Name: COLUMN customer_sales_area.shipping_condition; Type: COMMENT; Schema: public; Owner: cairn_integration_migrator
--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.customer_sales_area.shipping_condition IS 'KNVV-VSBED. How this customer wants goods to reach them, and the customer''s half of shipping point determination. Null is a customer who has said nothing: those are answered by the determination rows that name no condition.';


--
-- Name: COLUMN customer_sales_area.partial_delivery_indicator; Type: COMMENT; Schema: public; Owner: cairn_integration_migrator
--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.customer_sales_area.partial_delivery_indicator IS 'KNVV-KZTLF. How much of an item may go out at once: blank leaves it free to travel in pieces, C says an item is delivered complete or not at all. It is a rule about the item, where the complete-delivery flag beside it is a rule about the order.';


--
-- Name: COLUMN customer_sales_area.max_partial_deliveries; Type: COMMENT; Schema: public; Owner: cairn_integration_migrator
--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.customer_sales_area.max_partial_deliveries IS 'KNVV-ANTLF. How many times an item may be split across deliveries before the rest has to travel together. Zero is a customer who has said nothing about it, and it is read as no limit: a limit of zero would be a customer who can never be served, which is what the partial delivery indicator C is for.';


--
-- Name: COLUMN customer_sales_area.invoice_list_schedule; Type: COMMENT; Schema: public; Owner: cairn_integration_migrator
--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.customer_sales_area.invoice_list_schedule IS 'How often this partner''s invoices are grouped onto an invoice list: NONE (released to accounting on their own), WEEKLY or MONTHLY. It is the payer''s field and not the sold-to''s, because an invoice list is made out to the partner who pays.';


